{:spec/title "Workflow resume — emit :workflow/resumed naming the phase it resumes from and the phases it skips"

 :spec/description
 "`bb miniforge resume <id>` restarts a checkpointed run, but its event log
  never says so. The event exists end to end except for its producer:
  `:workflow/resumed` is in `event-type-registry.edn`, its schema is in
  `event_stream/recovery_draft_spec.clj`, its message
  (`\"Workflow resumed at {from-phase}; skipped: {skipping}\"`) is in the
  event-stream catalog, and `ai.miniforge.event-stream.interface/workflow-resumed`
  builds it. Nothing in production calls it, so a resumed run's log looks
  like a run that started mid-pipeline.

  Change: the resume command (`bases/cli/src/ai/miniforge/cli/main/commands/resume.clj`)
  publishes one `:workflow/resumed` event on the run's event stream after it
  has reconstructed the checkpoint, applied any `--from-phase` rewind
  (`apply-from-phase`), and before the pipeline runs. The event names the
  phase the run actually resumes at and the phases it skips.

  The resume phase is the one the command already prints as `Resuming from
  phase` (`resume-print-phase`): the FSM snapshot's current phase, or, on a
  snapshot-less or failed-checkpoint resume, the first phase of the pipeline
  `wr/trim-pipeline` leaves. The skipped phases are the pipeline phases
  before it. Neither is read off which phases have a checkpointed result:
  `reconstruct-context` counts only completed phases, so a failed or
  retrying phase with a checkpoint runs again, and `trim-pipeline` drops
  only the leading completed phases, so a completed phase after the first
  incomplete one also runs again. A resume that the command refuses (spec
  drift without --force, non-resumable status, an unknown or refused
  --from-phase) publishes nothing."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :bugfix
  :scope ["bases/cli/src/ai/miniforge/cli/main/commands/resume.clj"
          "bases/cli/test/ai/miniforge/cli/main/commands/resume_test.clj"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["Use the existing `es/workflow-resumed` constructor; add no new event type or schema"
  "Publish exactly once per accepted resume, before the pipeline starts"
  "A refused resume publishes no :workflow/resumed event"
  "Tests use an in-memory event stream; no real checkpoint directory under ~/.miniforge"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["An accepted resume publishes one :workflow/resumed event whose resume phase is the phase resume-print-phase reports"
  "The event's skipped phases are the pipeline phases before the resume phase, in pipeline order"
  "With no snapshot and completed phases [:explore :plan :verify] in a pipeline explore, plan, implement, verify, release, the resume phase is :implement and the skipped phases are [:explore :plan]"
  "A phase whose checkpointed result failed is the resume phase, not a skipped phase"
  "With --from-phase, the resume phase is the requested phase and the skipped phases are the pipeline phases before it"
  "The event validates against the :workflow/resumed schema in recovery_draft_spec.clj"
  "A resume refused for spec drift without --force publishes no :workflow/resumed event"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :high
  :axes #{:observation :dogfood-enabler}
  :theme :dogfood-resilience
  :rationale "Without the event, a resumed dogfood run cannot be told apart from a fresh one in the event log or the dashboard."
  :blocks []
  :blocked-by []}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
